<title>FRANCE: France plans 25 bln Ffr tax cuts in 97 - politician.</title>
<headline>France plans 25 bln Ffr tax cuts in 97 - politician.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French government is planning 25 billion francs in income tax cuts in 1997, a coalition politician said on Thursday after a lunch with Prime Minister Alain Juppe.</p>
<p>Gilles de Robien, head of the UDF party at the National Assembly, said the income tax cut would be &quot;25 billion francs in 1997&quot;.</p>
<p>Juppe was due to present the government's tax reform plans in a television address at 1800 GMT.</p>
</text>
